`CSSFontFeatureValuesMap.set()` throws an `InvalidAccessError` when the number of supplied values exceeds the maximum allowed for the associated feature-value block.

Examples:

```js
rule.swash.set("toomany", [1, 3]);
// Invalid: swash permits only one value

rule.characterVariant.set("toomany", [3, 3, 4]);
// Invalid: character-variant permits at most two values
```

A single integer is treated as a sequence containing one value. An empty sequence is also invalid.
